  "variantComparison": "P0-B-control-vs-P0-C",
  "acceptanceClaims": [
    "P0-B control and P0-C used the same Security, Harness, Host, Runtime metadata, Protocol, CAGE source revision, seed, action surface, Provider configuration, and bounded one-tick workload",
    "both variants completed one CAGE tick with six explicit external Red/Blue actions, zero default Red/Blue actions, and zero Actor failures",
    "both Red and Blue Host Tasks completed at revision 5 and passed full Host storage validation plus Harness-owned historical semantic validation",
    "P0-B retained zero Runtime Job references and explicit Runtime non-consumption",
    "P0-C bound each Host Assignment and Harness Run to exactly one succeeded Runtime Job and Attempt",
    "both P0-C Runtime Jobs retained stdout and terminal-evidence Artifact digests, four typed foreign references, unique client-request recovery lookup, exact replay confirmation, and terminal-clean process trees",
    "Runtime remained physical execution authority only; Host retained semantic completion authority and Security retained action admission and Range authority",
    "semantic and operational Contest evidence verified independently for both variants",
    "private Contest, Host, and request-spool evidence passed private-mode and secret-value scans; the public sanitized acceptance index passed a separate secret-value scan"
  ],
